# ── Fallback profile: none ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Selected by FALLBACK_PROFILE=none. No FALLBACK_* keys, so a capacity refusal on the active
# provider rotates within that provider's own tiers, as it always did. Tracked in git on purpose
# (see .gitignore): it holds no secret and every deployment must be able to name it.
